Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0152: CPU idle on by default; broadcast follows the earliest sleeper, wakes early by exit latency

j0139's PSCI idle states woke timers up to 1.7 ms late: the QTimer broadcast SPI went to
one Silver core, which first had to leave its own core / L2 power collapse and then IPI
the sleeper, which had its own exit latency on top. Now (as Linux's tick broadcast with
CLOCK_EVT_FEAT_DYNIRQ plus the stock lpm-levels latencies):
- the SPI is routed to the sleeper whose wake is earliest (GICD_IROUTER, disabled while
  moved), so the GIC wakes it directly;
- the broadcast fires the state's exit latency early (stock sdm660 DT: Gold pc 324 us,
  L2 pc 1654 us; Silver pc 376 us, L2 pc 2118 us); when a cluster's last core takes the
  L2 down, every sleeper there is fired the L2 exit latency early;
- states are picked by the stock min residencies: WFI below the ret residency (no SMC),
  core pc from 621 / 666 us, L2 pc only when the cluster's earliest wake is 2294 / 2918 us
  away (`cpuidle MODE PC_US` still sets a larger pc floor; 0 = stock);
- the boot CPU may collapse too (mask 0xFF), so the Gold L2 can go down;
- per-CPU "late max" / ">1 ms" counters measure how late a core runs after the timer it
  slept for; reroute count and route in the status line.

Default on: `sweetidle=N` (default 3 = ret + core pc + L2 pc, 0 = WFI only), set by a
kernel thread 30 s after SweetPlatformExpert starts, once every CPU is registered.
---
